<title>SRI LANKA: Tokyo Cement up on bonus news.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Cement up on bonus news.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Cement (Lanka) Ltd rose 3.45 percent or two rupees to 60, on 300 shares following a bonus announcement of one new share for every three held, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The price rise is directly linked to this morning's bonus announcement,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company's issued capital will rise to 10 million shares from 7.5 million shares, after the issue.</p>
<p>Tokyo Cement manufactures Mitsui brand cement in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
